# Trivy ignore entries — EXAMPLE.
#
# Copy to your repository root as `.trivyignore`.
# Implements: docs/07-security/vulnerability-management.md
#             docs/10-governance/exception-management.md
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERY ENTRY IN THIS FILE IS AN EXCEPTION TO A SECURITY CONTROL.
#
# It must record: the finding, why it does not apply, what compensates for
# it meanwhile, who approved it, and when it expires.
#
# An entry without those is a permanent, invisible weakening of a control —
# invisible precisely because it works.
#
# The file format has no concept of expiry. Nothing here enforces it. An
# external check must compare the Expires dates against today and fail the
# build, or these entries are permanent by construction.
# `TBD` — whether that check exists.
#
# An expired exception is a CONTROL FAILURE, not a default extension.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Example entry: not exploitable in this context ------------------------
# CVE-0000-11111
# Package:      example-lib 1.2.3
# Severity:     HIGH
# Finding:      Remote code execution via the XML parsing path
# Justification: This application does not parse XML. The vulnerable code
#               path is unreachable — verified by inspection on 2026-08-16.
# Compensating: None required; the path is not invoked
# Approved by:  Security owner (role)
# Raised:       2026-08-16
# Expires:      TBD
# Remediation:  Upstream fix expected in 1.3.0; upgrade when released
CVE-0000-11111


# --- Example entry: no fix available yet -----------------------------------
# CVE-0000-22222
# Package:      base-os-package 2.4.1
# Severity:     CRITICAL
# Finding:      Privilege escalation
# Justification: No fixed version exists. The container runs as a non-root
#               user with no capabilities, which the exploit requires
# Compensating: Non-root execution; read-only root filesystem
# Approved by:  Security owner (role)
# Raised:       2026-08-16
# Expires:      TBD — short. Re-evaluate as soon as a fix ships
# Remediation:  Rebuild on a patched base image
CVE-0000-22222


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must NEVER appear here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   - A bare CVE identifier with no surrounding record. Nobody can evaluate
#     it later, including the person who added it
#   - A wildcard or blanket suppression. Scope is per finding, per package
#   - "Temporary, will fix later" without a date. That is how an exception
#     becomes permanent
#   - An entry added to unblock a release without an approver. That is a
#     self-service bypass of a security control
#
# If this file is growing, the signal is not that the scanner is noisy. It is
# that findings are being recorded rather than fixed — the metrics improve
# while the exposure does not.
